  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 8909a7b854c460945b7273a620ed017e, type: 3}
  m_Name: PoI_03_Mr Watson
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  speakerName: Mr Watson
  characterAvatar: {fileID: 0}
  arrivalPrompt: "As a choirister in the 1970s, a lifetime of memories about the
    Cathedral stays with Mr Watson. Even after the earthquakes, he has continued
    to follow the Cathedral's story. He knows its stories intimately \u2014 and believes
    that even its stones have stories to tell."
  arrivalButtonText: Meet Mr Watson
  dialogueLines:
  - Hello, young friend. What a pleasure to see you here.
  - I forgot to introduce myself. My name is Louis Watson. People call me Mr Watson.
    I used to sing in the Cathedral Choir when I was a young boy, and later when
    I became a teacher, I brought my students here every year.
  - There were some naughty ones wandering and missing their ways that I had to remind
    them to look for the tallest spire to find the right way.
  - I have so many memories of this Cathedral. Some are carved in stone, some can
    be seen in its windows, and some can still be heard in music. Since you are here
    today, why don't you spend a little time with me so I can show you around?
  - I will keep you company, just in case you need a hand. I can tell you what I
    remember about each spot you explore. Take your time, and remember you can always
    pause, put down the tablet, and take in the real space around you.
  alignmentPrompt: 
  alignmentButtonText: 
  interactionInstruction: Three memories are waiting in this space \u2014 carved
    in stone, reflected in glass, and carried in music. Explore them at your own
    pace, and feel free to look around and touch your surroundings.
  interactionButtonText: Start Exploring
  reflectionPrompt: '"What do you think makes a place worth remembering?"'
  reflectionButtonText: Continue
